1
00:00:00,112 --> 00:00:00,625
Part three.

2
00:00:01,038 --> 00:00:02,050
AI is not smart.

3
00:00:02,462 --> 00:00:03,550
Cuban says it flatly.

4
00:00:03,962 --> 00:00:04,525
In his view,

5
00:00:04,950 --> 00:00:07,550
AI uses statistics to predict the next word.

6
00:00:07,962 --> 00:00:09,825
It's predictive, not deterministic.

7
00:00:10,238 --> 00:00:12,538
Ask four different AIs the same question,

8
00:00:12,850 --> 00:00:14,262
and you get four different answers.

9
00:00:14,675 --> 00:00:16,038
Change your question slightly,

10
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:18,412
and the same AI changes its answer.

11
00:00:18,838 --> 00:00:19,062
That,

12
00:00:19,462 --> 00:00:21,600
he says, doesn't work in the real world.

13
00:00:22,012 --> 00:00:24,338
AI doesn't know the consequences of its actions.

14
00:00:24,750 --> 00:00:26,112
It has no built-in ethics.

15
00:00:26,525 --> 00:00:27,762
And it's always out of date,

16
00:00:27,975 --> 00:00:29,938
because the moment a model is released,

17
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:31,800
today's conversations aren't in it.

18
00:00:32,225 --> 00:00:33,213
His favourite example.

19
00:00:33,638 --> 00:00:35,775
Put him at a busy four-way intersection,

20
00:00:36,050 --> 00:00:38,113
with the best AI model on his phone

21
00:00:38,350 --> 00:00:39,875
and a seeing-eye dog beside him.

22
00:00:40,288 --> 00:00:41,800
He'd let the dog walk him across the

23
00:00:41,812 --> 00:00:42,588
street first.

24
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,200
Or picture a two-year-old in a high chair.

25
00:00:45,625 --> 00:00:47,400
The toddler knows that if the sippy cup

26
00:00:47,412 --> 00:00:48,438
goes over the edge,

27
00:00:48,750 --> 00:00:49,550
mom comes running.

28
00:00:49,975 --> 00:00:52,088
Cuban says AI is never going to figure

29
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:52,538
that out.

30
00:00:52,950 --> 00:00:54,625
Even the scary hacking stories,

31
00:00:54,812 --> 00:00:56,600
he says, aren't intelligence.

32
00:00:57,012 --> 00:00:58,175
Nothing new was invented.

33
00:00:58,588 --> 00:01:01,137
AI just tried every known trick in every

34
00:01:01,150 --> 00:01:02,325
possible combination.

35
00:01:02,750 --> 00:01:03,675
That's brute force.

36
00:01:04,088 --> 00:01:06,200
And defenders can use the same brute force

37
00:01:06,212 --> 00:01:07,738
to find their own holes first.

38
00:01:08,162 --> 00:01:08,975
So he's not a doomer.

39
00:01:09,412 --> 00:01:11,062
He says he's more afraid of what people

40
00:01:11,075 --> 00:01:13,600
do out of fear and misunderstanding than of

41
00:01:13,612 --> 00:01:14,550
what AI will do.

42
00:01:14,975 --> 00:01:16,200
Bartlett pushes back hard.

43
00:01:16,625 --> 00:01:18,625
These technologies look exponential.

44
00:01:19,038 --> 00:01:20,712
His own Tesla drives itself,

45
00:01:21,012 --> 00:01:23,262
and its crash rate is reportedly lower than

46
00:01:23,275 --> 00:01:24,238
a human driver's.

47
00:01:24,650 --> 00:01:25,362
At some point,

48
00:01:25,550 --> 00:01:26,363
doesn't the curve win?

49
00:01:26,788 --> 00:01:27,512
Cuban's answer:

50
00:01:28,012 --> 00:01:29,625
as long as there's a delay between the

51
00:01:29,638 --> 00:01:31,125
real world and the model,

52
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:32,600
people keep the edge.

53
00:01:33,012 --> 00:01:35,788
And yet, this same skeptic has twenty-five AI

54
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:36,788
agents on his phone.
